# hope-mlflow-config (TASK-822)
#
# DESTINATION: hope-v2-deployment, `deployment/k8s/base/config/mlflow.env`,
# wired as a `configMapGenerator` entry named `hope-mlflow-config`.
#
# NON-SECRET keys only. Everything with credential material in it —
# MLFLOW_BACKEND_STORE_URI (carries the Postgres password) and the scoped MinIO
# key pair — lives in the hand-applied `hope-secrets` Secret, because Argo CD's
# AppProject BLACKLISTS `{group: "", kind: Secret}` and may never manage one.
#
# A generator, not a plain ConfigMap: the content hash lands in the pod template,
# so editing this file actually rolls MLflow. A plain ConfigMap edit would not.

# The MinIO endpoint MLflow proxies artifacts to. Also promoted to a
# NON-OPTIONAL configMapKeyRef on the Deployment so CI's check-config-refs.py
# can see it — envFrom keys are invisible to that gate, and the silent fallback
# is dangerous: absent, boto3 does not fail, it resolves the DEFAULT AWS
# endpoint and ships our artifacts at s3.amazonaws.com.
MLFLOW_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=http://minio.taphuynh.dev:9000
